  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Nanduri Hanumantha Rao vs State Of Ap on 13 September, 2019 Author: U. Durga Prasad Rao Bench: U. Durga Prasad Rao Hon'Ble Sri Justice U. Durga Prasad Rao Criminal Petition No.5059 Of 2019 Order:",
    "facts": "The petitioner/A5 seeks to quash the proceedings against him in Crime No.190 of 2019 of Thulluru Police Station, Guntur District, registered for the offences under Sections 270, 273, 328 and 420 of IPC and Sections 56, 57 and 63 of Food Safety and Standards Act (for short, 'FSS Act'). 2. The allegations against the petitioner briefly are that on 23.06.2019, when the complainant along with his staff conducting search at outskirts of Lingayapalem Village, Seed Access Road, on suspicion, caught the accused and found the banned tobacco products in their possession and hence, seized the same and registered a case in Crime No.190 of 2019 of Thulluru Police Station, for the offences stated supra. 3.",
    "arguments": "Learned counsel for petitioner while denying the FIR allegations would submit that even if the prosecution case is accepted to be true, tobacco products would not fall within the definition of Section 3(j) of FSS Act and therefore, the Police are not authorized to register the crime, investigate and file charge sheet and therefore, registration of the FIR is contrary to the provisions of FSS Act.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "Learned counsel for petitioner while denying the FIR allegations would submit that even if the prosecution case is accepted to be true, tobacco products would not fall within the definition of Section 3(j) of FSS Act and therefore, the Police are not authorized to register the crime, investigate and file charge sheet and therefore, registration of the FIR is contrary to the provisions of FSS Act.",
    "respondent_arguments": "",
    "other_lawyer_arguments": ""
  },
